@startuml Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Hybrid Model Sequence Diagram

/'
    Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Hybrid Model Sequence Diagram
    ========================================================

    This diagram demonstrates the hybrid workflow-data stream execution model,
    showing how tasks coordinate through both explicit dependencies and implicit
    data flow dependencies.

    Key Concepts:
    - TASK_TYPE_LEGACY: Only task dependencies, immediate execution
    - TASK_TYPE_HYBRID: Task + data dependencies, flexible coordination
    - TASK_TYPE_DATAFLOW: Only data dependencies, event-driven execution

    Execution Patterns:
    - Producer-Consumer: Data producers write to streams
    - Pipeline Processing: Data flows through processing stages
    - Hybrid Coordination: Mix of dependency types for complex workflows

    Generated: 2026-01-05
    Version: 1.0
'/

title Parallel Pipeline Data Flow Hybrid Model Sequence Diagram

actor User as "Application"
participant WF as "ParallelWorkflow"
participant Checker as "DependencyChecker"
participant Task1 as "SensorTask\n(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)"
participant Task2 as "ProcessorTask\n(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)"
participant Task3 as "AlertHandler\n(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)"
participant Task4 as "DecisionTask\n(TASK_TYPE_DATAFLOW)"
participant DS as "DataStreamService"
participant Stream1 as "sensor_data\n(FIFO, capacity=10)"
participant Stream2 as "processed_data\n(LATEST, capacity=5)"
participant Stream3 as "alert_data\n(FIFO, capacity=20)"

== Workflow Initialization ==
User -> WF: parallel_workflow_init_ex(enable_data_streams=1)
activate WF
WF -> DS: data_stream_service_create()
activate DS
DS --> WF: data_stream_service
WF --> User: workflow ready

== Task Configuration ==
User -> Task1: parallel_task_init(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)
Task1 -> Task1: set_type(HYBRID)
User -> Task1: parallel_task_add_output_stream(sensor_data)
Task1 -> DS: register_output_stream(sensor_data)
DS --> Task1: stream registered

User -> Task2: parallel_task_init(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)
Task2 -> Task2: set_type(HYBRID)
User -> Task2: parallel_task_add_input_stream(sensor_data)
Task2 -> DS: register_input_stream(sensor_data)
User -> Task2: parallel_task_add_output_stream(processed_data)
Task2 -> DS: register_output_stream(processed_data)
User -> Task2: parallel_task_add_dependency(Task1.task_id)
Task2 -> Task2: add_task_dependency(Task1)

User -> Task3: parallel_task_init(TASK_TYPE_HYBRID)
Task3 -> Task3: set_type(HYBRID)
User -> Task3: parallel_task_add_input_stream(alert_data)
Task3 -> DS: register_input_stream(alert_data)

User -> Task4: parallel_task_init(TASK_TYPE_DATAFLOW)
Task4 -> Task4: set_type(DATAFLOW)
User -> Task4: parallel_task_add_input_stream(processed_data)
Task4 -> DS: register_input_stream(processed_data)
User -> Task4: parallel_task_add_dependency(Task2.task_id)
Task4 -> Task4: add_task_dependency(Task2)

== Workflow Start ==
User -> WF: parallel_workflow_start()
WF -> WF: set_state(PWORKFLOW_RUNNING)

== Dependency Resolution Phase ==
note over WF, Task4
    **Dependency Resolution Logic:**

    **Task1 (HYBRID)**: No task dependencies ✓
    → Ready to start immediately

    **Task2 (HYBRID)**: Depends on Task1 ✗
    → Waiting for Task1 completion

    **Task3 (HYBRID)**: No task dependencies ✓
    → Ready to start immediately

    **Task4 (DATAFLOW)**: Depends on Task2 ✗
    → Waiting for Task2 completion + data availability
end note

WF -> Checker: check_all_task_dependencies()
Checker -> Task1: check_dependencies()
Task1 -> Task1: check_task_dependencies()
Task1 --> Checker: no_dependencies ✓
Checker -> Task3: check_dependencies()
Task3 -> Task3: check_task_dependencies()
Task3 --> Checker: no_dependencies ✓
Checker -> Task2: check_dependencies()
Task2 -> Task2: check_task_dependencies()
Task2 --> Checker: has_unmet_dependencies ✗
Checker -> Task4: check_dependencies()
Task4 -> Task4: check_task_dependencies()
Task4 --> Checker: has_unmet_dependencies ✗
Checker --> WF: ready_tasks = [Task1, Task3]

== Concurrent Execution Phase 1 ==
WF -> WF: acquire_concurrency_semaphore()
WF -> Task1: parallel_task_start()
activate Task1
Task1 -> Task1: create_execution_thread()
Task1 --> WF: task_started

WF -> WF: acquire_concurrency_semaphore()
WF -> Task3: parallel_task_start()
activate Task3
Task3 -> Task3: create_execution_thread()
Task3 --> WF: task_started

== Task Execution (Phase 1) ==
Task1 -> Task1: execute_sensor_task()
Task1 -> Stream1: data_stream_write(sensor_reading)
activate Stream1
Stream1 -> Stream1: enqueue_data(sensor_reading)
Stream1 --> Task1: data_written
Task1 -> Task1: set_state(PTASK_COMPLETED)
Task1 -> WF: mark_task_completed(Task1)
deactivate Task1

== Hybrid Dependency Check ==
WF -> Checker: check_task_dependencies()
Checker -> Task2: check_dependencies()
Task2 -> Task2: check_task_dependencies()
Task2 --> Checker: task_dependencies_met ✓

note right: Task2 has HYBRID dependencies:
- Task dependency: Task1 ✓ completed
- Data dependency: sensor_data stream

Checker -> Stream1: data_stream_has_data()
Stream1 --> Checker: data_available ✓
Checker --> WF: Task2_ready ✓

== Concurrent Execution Phase 2 ==
WF -> WF: release_concurrency_semaphore()
WF -> Task2: parallel_task_start()
activate Task2
Task2 -> Task2: create_execution_thread()
Task2 --> WF: task_started

== Data Flow Processing ==
Task2 -> Task2: execute_processor_task()
Task2 -> Stream1: data_stream_read(sensor_data)
Stream1 -> Stream1: dequeue_data()
Stream1 --> Task2: sensor_data
deactivate Stream1

Task2 -> Task2: process_sensor_data()
note right: Processing generates alerts\nwhen temperature > 28°C

Task2 -> Stream3: data_stream_write(alert_data)
activate Stream3
Stream3 -> Stream3: enqueue_data(alert)
Stream3 --> Task2: alert_written

Task2 -> Stream2: data_stream_write(processed_data)
activate Stream2
Stream2 -> Stream2: enqueue_data(result)
Stream2 --> Task2: data_written
deactivate Stream2

Task2 -> Task2: set_state(PTASK_COMPLETED)
Task2 -> WF: mark_task_completed(Task2)
deactivate Task2

== Task3 Data-Driven Execution ==
note over Task3
    Task3 (HYBRID) is already running.
    It checks for alert_data periodically.
end note

Task3 -> Stream3: data_stream_read(alert_data, timeout=500ms)
Stream3 -> Stream3: check_available_data()
Stream3 --> Task3: alert_data_available
Task3 -> Task3: process_alert()
Task3 -> Task3: continue_monitoring()

== DataFlow Task Activation ==
WF -> Checker: check_task_dependencies()
Checker -> Task4: check_dependencies()
Task4 -> Task4: check_task_dependencies()
Task4 --> Checker: task_dependencies_met ✓

note right: Task4 has DATAFLOW dependencies:
- Task dependency: Task2 ✓ completed
- Data dependency: processed_data stream

Checker -> Stream2: data_stream_has_data()
Stream2 --> Checker: data_available ✓
Checker --> WF: Task4_ready ✓

== Concurrent Execution Phase 3 ==
WF -> WF: acquire_concurrency_semaphore()
WF -> Task4: parallel_task_start()
activate Task4
Task4 -> Task4: create_execution_thread()
Task4 --> WF: task_started

== Final Data Processing ==
Task4 -> Task4: execute_decision_task()
Task4 -> Stream2: data_stream_read(processed_data)
Stream2 -> Stream2: dequeue_data()
Stream2 --> Task4: processed_data
deactivate Stream2

Task4 -> Task4: analyze_processed_data()
Task4 -> Task4: make_decision()
Task4 -> Task4: set_state(PTASK_COMPLETED)
Task4 -> WF: mark_task_completed(Task4)
deactivate Task4

== Completion Phase ==
WF -> WF: check_all_tasks_completed()
WF -> WF: set_state(PWORKFLOW_COMPLETED)
WF --> User: workflow_completed

Task3 -> Task3: complete_monitoring()
Task3 -> Task3: set_state(PTASK_COMPLETED)
Task3 -> WF: mark_task_completed(Task3)
deactivate Task3

deactivate Stream3
deactivate DS
deactivate WF

note over User, Task4
    **Hybrid Execution Summary:**

    **Phase 1 (Concurrent):**
    - Task1 & Task3 start immediately (no dependencies)
    - Task1 produces sensor_data
    - Task3 monitors alert_data (empty initially)

    **Phase 2 (Dependency Triggered):**
    - Task1 completion + sensor_data availability
    - Task2 starts processing
    - Task2 produces processed_data + alert_data

    **Phase 3 (Data Driven):**
    - Task2 completion + processed_data availability
    - Task4 starts decision making
    - Task3 processes available alerts

    **Key Benefits:**
    - Mixed dependency models for flexibility
    - Data-driven execution for responsiveness
    - Concurrent processing for performance
end note

@enduml
